INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-art-of-dosa', 'the-art-of-dosa', 'The art of dosa', 'The ingredient', 'Rice, lentils, a night of patience and a hot tawa. Why something so simple takes a lifetime to get right.', '/assets/v2/journal/dosa.webp', 'A ladle spreading dosa batter in a wide circle on a hot tawa', 'A dosa begins the night before. Rice and urad dal are soaked, ground and left to ferment, and by morning the batter has risen, turned a little sour and taken on the faint sweetness that makes a good dosa taste like more than the sum of its parts.

## The tawa

Then comes the part everyone watches. A ladle of batter, a quick spiral outward from the centre, and the edges begin to lift almost immediately. Too cool and the dosa sticks; too hot and it sets before it spreads.

## Benne

Benne means butter, and a benne dosa is the thicker, softer, richer cousin of the paper-thin dosa most people picture: crisp at the edges, tender in the middle, glossy with butter or ghee.

> A dosa rewards attention. It is ready when it tells you it is.

Served with sambhar and chutneys, or with a Mangalorean ghee roast or a Chettinad masala, it is still the simplest and most satisfying breakfast we know.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-10-04', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-no-clock', 'why-breakfast-should-never-have-a-clock', 'Why breakfast should never have a clock', 'The story', 'Dosa at noon, eggs at four, coffee whenever. A small argument for eating breakfast on your own time.', '/assets/v2/journal/no-clock.webp', 'Afternoon light falling across a breakfast table with coffee and idli', 'Somewhere along the way breakfast acquired a deadline. Order before eleven, or the kitchen moves on.

By the sea, days keep a different time. Some mornings start at dawn with the fishing boats; some start at noon after a late night. Neither deserves a lesser plate.

## Breakfast, all day

So breakfast stays on the menu from the moment we open to the moment we close. Idli at two in the afternoon. A masala omelette at four. Coffee whenever you would like another.

> The best meal of the day should not depend on what time you woke up.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-10-03', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-story-behind-the-spice', 'the-story-behind-the-spice', 'The story behind the spice', 'The ingredient', 'Pepper, chilli, curry leaf and mustard seed: the small things that make South Indian food taste like itself.', '/assets/v2/journal/spice.webp', 'Dried red chillies, black pepper, curry leaves and mustard seeds on dark stone', 'Long before anyone wrote down a recipe, this coast traded in flavour. Pepper from the Western Ghats, cardamom from the hills, coconut from every shoreline.

## The tempering

In a South Indian kitchen the spice often arrives last. Mustard seeds crackle in hot oil, curry leaves spit and turn glossy, dried chillies darken, and the whole lot is poured over a dish at the very end. It is called a tadka or a tempering, and it is the reason a bowl of sambhar smells the way it does.

## Podi

Then there is podi, the roasted lentil and chilli powder some call gunpowder. Mixed with ghee or butter, it turns a plain idli into something you think about for the rest of the day.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-10-02', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-south-to-coast', 'from-the-south-to-the-coast', 'From the South to the coast', 'The coast', 'Mangalore, Bangalore, Chettinad and Udupi on one table in Anjuna.', '/assets/v2/journal/south-to-coast.webp', 'A table by the coast laid with South Indian breakfast dishes in morning light', 'Read the breakfast menu slowly and it becomes a map. Ghee roast from Mangalore. Tatte idli from Bangalore. Chettinad masala from the deep south of Tamil Nadu. Uppit and sheera from Udupi temple kitchens.

## A coastal table

Each travelled its own road to get here. Brought together in Anjuna, they sit beside the sea that connects them all, and beside the eggs, toast and bowls that the coast has made its own.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-10-01', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-portuguese-coast', 'a-little-portuguese-in-the-coast', 'A little Portuguese in the coast', 'The story', 'Poi, choris and a few centuries of exchange: the Portuguese thread in Goan breakfast.', '/assets/v2/journal/portuguese.webp', 'Soft poi bread and smoked choris on a wooden board', 'Goa''s breakfast tables still carry a Portuguese accent. The poi, a soft, hollow, flour-dusted bread, came with the bakers who followed the ships. The choris, a spiced and smoked sausage, owes its name and its vinegar to the same journey.

## On the menu

You will find them in a Portuguese omelette with smoked choris and onion jam, in choris on toast, and under almost every egg we serve, on char-grilled poi.

> Same ocean, a few new flavours.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-09-30', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-inside-our-kitchen', 'inside-our-kitchen', 'Inside our kitchen', 'The people', 'Batter, ghee, a hot tawa and a coffee pot that never quite empties.', '/assets/v2/journal/kitchen.webp', 'Hands turning a dosa on a cast iron tawa in a warm kitchen', 'A breakfast kitchen moves to a rhythm. Batter is stirred and ladled, idli pots steam, eggs crack, the tawa is wiped and seasoned between every dosa, and the coffee pot is never quite empty.

## Iron, clay and grill

Some things meet cast iron, some arrive in clay, some come off the grill. Each changes the food a little: the char on a poi, the softness of a tatte idli in its clay pot, the edge on a dosa.

Come in, find a table and stay awhile.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-09-29', 1);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO journal_posts (id, slug, title, category, excerpt, cover, cover_alt, body, author, published_at, published) VALUES ('post-crab-journey', 'the-crab-journey-coming-soon', 'The crab journey: coming soon', 'The crab', 'Something is growing. Our crab cultivation project is underway, and it is not on the menu yet.', '/assets/v2/journal/crab-journey.webp', 'Still mangrove water at dawn with roots reflected on the surface', 'Our crab cultivation project is underway.

It is a slow undertaking, with calm water, patience and close attention, and it is not something we will rush to the table.

## Coming soon

Soon, the journey from cultivation to kitchen will become part of the Sal Marinho experience. Until then, it stays in the water.', 'The Sal Marinho kitchen', '2026-09-28', 1);
